Generate the autocompletion script for powershell.

To load completions in your current shell session:

	flate completion powershell | Out-String | Invoke-Expression

To load completions for every new session, add the output of the above command
to your powershell profile.

Usage:
  flate completion powershell [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help[=true|false]              help for powershell
      --no-descriptions[=true|false]   disable completion descriptions

Global Flags:
      --log-level string           Set log level: debug,info,warn,error [env: FLATE_LOG_LEVEL] (default "error")
      --no-progress[=true|false]   Hide live progress on stderr [env: FLATE_NO_PROGRESS]
